{
	"_about": "Hand-made markets. remoteness: how hard the market is to reach; a market is open only when the player's transport tier reaches it (max_remoteness in transport.json). A run starts with the markets that the first tier reaches. population and income: the population and income of the market at the start of a run (see market in balance.json). More remote markets have more income, so they pay more. prices: color id to the base price, the money one widget of that color sells for at demand 1 and at the reference income. Demand (see balance.json) changes the price. Each market has a higher base price for some colors. generator: the rules that make markets after the hand-made ones, so that the game has no end (see MarketGenerator). The game makes generated markets until at least closed_markets_shown markets are closed to the player's transport tier. A tier that reaches any remoteness, such as the portal, closes no market, so with it the game counts the markets that no link goes to. Generated market n has the remoteness of the most remote hand-made market plus remoteness_step times n. Its population is population_base plus population_per_remoteness times its remoteness, and its income is income_base plus income_per_remoteness times its remoteness, each times a random factor from 1 - spread to 1 + spread. Its base price of each color is the lowest base price of that color in the hand-made markets, and favored_colors random colors have favored_price_factor times that price. Its name is one of name_starts and one of name_ends. The run's seed sets the random values. PLACEHOLDER remoteness values, populations, incomes, prices, and generator rules until playtests set them.",
